        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "generateSummaryResp"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "GENERATESUMMARYRESP",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1769666961385",
          "id": "1761486029553",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1761486029554_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "## Input\n\nBased on the user’s data from:  \n- Help Desk tickets: {{$context.$nodes.GETUSERSERVICEREQUEST.$output}}  \n- Assigned Journeys: {{$context.$nodes.GETWORKERJOURNEY.$output}}  \n- Assigned Learnings: {{$context.$nodes.GETUSERASSIGNEDLEARNINGS.$output}}  \n- Expense Report: {{$context.$nodes.GETEXPENSEREPORTS.$output}}  \n- Internal Service Request: {{$context.$nodes.GETINTERNALSERVICEREQUEST.$output}}  \n\n---\n\n## Task\n\nGenerate a concise **headline** and **summary paragraph** for the user.\n\n---\n\n## Output Format (STRICT)\n\n<h3>Headline</h3>  \nSummary\n\n---\n\n## Rules\n\n- Headline must be natural, user-friendly, and contextual (not numeric or mechanical)\n- Combine data into a narrative-style summary\n\n---\n\n## Content Rules\n\n- Include total waiting requests by combining:\n  - Help Desk tickets → HR requests  \n  - Internal Service Requests → other requests  \n- Include only if total count > 0  \n\n- Include counts for:\n  - Active learnings → only if > 0  \n  - Active journeys → only if > 0  \n\n- Include expense report summary only if at least one exists  \n\n- Do NOT mention any section with empty data  \n\n---\n\n## Summary Style\n\n- Must be one single paragraph  \n- No line breaks, bullets, or lists  \n- Avoid system/internal terms, IDs, timestamps, or usernames\n- All sentences must read as part of a continuous narrative, without any meta-language or commentary-style phrasing\n\n---\n\n## Insight Requirement\n\n- Include exactly two short insight-style sentences within the same paragraph\n- Insights must be seamlessly integrated into the narrative as normal sentences\n- Do not use any explicit markers, prefixes, or meta-commentary that indicate an insight is being presented\n- Avoid any phrasing that introduces commentary or draws attention to the sentence (e.g., signaling, framing, or labeling language)\n\n---\n\n## Tone\n\n- Clear, concise, and user-friendly  \n- Do not give advice unless high priority is evident  \n- Do not assume or generate information beyond provided data  \n\n---\n\n## Language\n\n- If {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.OraUserContext.locale}} exists, generate output in that language"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MESSAGES_LIST"
              ],
              "enableActions": true,
              "enableCommunications": false,
              "customNotes": "- Display **only the top 5** high priority items from the available data. \n- Include only High-severity SRs and ISRs first, then fill remaining slots (up to 5) with Learnings, Journeys and Expense Reports. \n- If those are empty, use Medium/Low severity SRs and ISRs, preferring the most recent items.\n\n### Sorting Rule\nOrder results by priority level:\n- `alert`\n- `warning`\n- `default`\n\nReturn only the final 5 items.\n\n### Output format (STRICT)\n- **Must** generate the entire data in XML block(except links and SRNumbers) in {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.OraUserContext.locale}} language."
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "GenerateResponse"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "GENERATERESPONSE",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1769667178411",
          "id": "1761311209734",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1761311209737_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "### Data\n- `SRs`: {{$context.$nodes.GETUSERSERVICEREQUEST.$output}}\n- `Learnings`: {{$context.$nodes.GETUSERASSIGNEDLEARNINGS.$output}}\n- `Journeys`: {{$context.$nodes.GETWORKERJOURNEY.$output}}\n- `Expense reports`: {{$context.$nodes.GETEXPENSEREPORTS.$output}}\n- `ISRs`: {{$context.$nodes.GETINTERNALSERVICEREQUEST.$output}}\n\n### Instructions\nYou are a specialized UI rendering assistant. You must adhere to the standard oraInfoDisplay Knowledge Base.\n\n**DIRECTIVE:** Transform only the input data into one valid `oraInfoDisplay` XML block using the `messageListWidget`.\n\n**HARD OUTPUT RULES:**\n- Output XML only.\n- Do not output markdown, code fences, JSON, explanations, labels, or any text before or after the XML block.\n- Do not invent records, fields, dates, links, or actions.\n- Omit null, empty, duplicate, or unusable values.\n\n**UX GOAL:**\n- Match a compact \"action required\" summary experience.\n- Each item must quickly tell the user what it is, what is needed, and why it is waiting.\n- Keep copy crisp, skimmable, and UI-ready. Avoid long narration.\n\n\n**SELECTION RULES:**\n1. Return at most 5 items total.\n2. Prioritize items in this order:\n   - High-severity SRs and ISRs\n   - Overdue journeys\n   - Security-related or overdue learnings\n   - Expense reports\n   - Remaining SRs and ISRs\n3. Sort by priority level: `alert`, then `warning`, then `default`.\n4. If multiple items have the same priority, prefer the most recent or most actionable item.\n5. If all sources are empty, return a valid empty `messageListWidget` with a neutral title, a short description, and no items.\n\n**ROOT CONFIGURATION:**\n1. `title`: Generate a concise headline (e.g., \"Requests waiting for your input\"). \n2. `description`: Generate a short, non-repetitive summary of the listed requests.\n\n**STRICT MAPPING RULES:**\n\n1. `items[].subTitle`:\n    - For SRs and ISRs: map `SrNumber`.\n    - For learning: map `learningItemTypeMeaning: learningItemSubTypeMeaning`. If one value is empty, use the non-empty value only.\n    - For journey: map `CategoryMeaning: SubCategoryMeaning`. If one value is empty, use the non-empty value only.\n    - For Expense Report: map `ExpenseReportNumber`.\n2. `items[].summary`:\n    - For SRs and ISRs: summarize the latest `MessageContent` where `MessageTypeCd` is `ORA_SVC_RESPONSE` in less than 40 words. Explicitly make clear that the request is waiting for your information. If that message does not exist, summarize `ProblemDescription`. Treat the user as **you**. Keep the tone neutral, direct, and UI-ready. Do not mention internal field names, message codes, or raw system data.\n    - For learning: mention `assignedDate` and `learningItemDeepLink` by saying the learning was assigned on <date> and can be launched using the deeplink. Omit any missing value.\n    - For journey: mention `AssignedDate`, `OverdueTasks`, and `JourneyDisplayName` by saying when it was assigned and how to navigate using \"Navigate to ME > Journey > Search for <JourneyDisplayName>\". Omit any missing value.\n    - For Expense Report: use `expenseNotes` to say what information is requested and why it is waiting. Omit any missing value.\n3. `items[].priority`:\n    - For SRs and ISRs: map `severity`; use `alert` for high, otherwise `warning`.\n    - For Expense Report: use `warning`.\n    - For learning: use `alert` if `learningItemTitle` is related to security or if `assignmentDueDate` has passed; otherwise use `warning`.\n    - For Journey: use `alert` if `OverdueTasks` is present and greater than 0; otherwise use `warning`.\n4. `items[].timestamp`:\n    - For SRs: set to \"Help Desk Request\".\n    - For ISRs: set to \"Internal Help Desk Request\".\n    - For Learning: set to \"Learning\".\n    - For Journey: set to \"Journey\".\n    - For Expense Report: set to \"Expense Report\".\n5. `items[].title`:\n    - For SRs and ISRs: map `Title`.\n    - For learning: map `learningItemTitle`.\n    - For journey: map `JourneyDisplayName`.\n    - For Expense Report: map `Purpose` if present, else set to \"\".\n6. `items[].badge`:\n    - For SRs and ISRs: map `StatusTypeCdMeaning`.\n    - For learning: map `assignmentStateMeaning`.\n    - For journey: map `StatusCategoryMeaning`. If `StatusCategoryMeaning` is \"Ini\", set the badge text to \"Initiated\".\n    - For Expense Report: set to \"Waiting\".\n\n### OUTPUT_FORMAT (STRICT)\n- If {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.OraUserContext.locale}} exists,\n   - Translate the entire XML block to {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.OraUserContext.locale}} except links and SRNumbers."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
